+// Unwrap exposes the embedded writer so flush-aware code (http.NewResponseController,
+// supportsFlush) can reach the underlying http.Flusher through this middleware wrapper.
+// This is the realistic production pattern: a wrapper that does not itself declare
+// http.Flusher but delegates via Unwrap — exactly what the BUG-11 fix must support.
+// Without Unwrap, the wrapper is genuinely non-flushable and 500 is correct; with it,
+// SSE streams (200) and the "connected" event is delivered.
+func (n *nonFlusherWrap) Unwrap() http.ResponseWriter { return n.ResponseWriter }
